# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output.
#
# The `!dist/.gitkeep` negation below does NOT work and never has: the repository
# root `.gitignore` excludes `dist/` as a *directory*, and git cannot re-include a
# path whose parent directory is excluded. Verified 2026-07-31 (#9603) — `git add
# crates/maekon-web/frontend/dist/.gitkeep` is a no-op without `-f`.
#
# Consequence, and the reason this is spelled out rather than deleted: a fresh
# clone has no `dist/` at all, so `cargo check -p maekon-app` fails outright with
# "The `frontendDist` configuration is set to ... but this path doesn't exist"
# before compiling a single line of app code. Building the frontend first is a
# hard prerequisite, not an optimization — see the from-source setup in
# `../../../README.md`. Tracking a `.gitkeep` would not fix it either: vite
# defaults to `emptyOutDir: true`, so every build would delete it again.
dist/*
!dist/.gitkeep

# Rust/Cargo build output generated by frontend-side checks
target/

